    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1578">

                <pb facs="1003" n="887" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg887"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/52.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihtiahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-15T13:00:00-07:04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 15, 1914, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s April 14, 5 p.m. Constitutionalist Secretary Foreign Affairs Fabela
                    has replied verbally that consistently with principles already enunciated his
                    government can not accept our mediation in Radke’s case because of the fact that
                    there is at Chihuahua German Consular Officer through whom such representations
                    should be made to Carranza. He calls attention in this connection to notes
                    already sent to the Department through Carothers and Simpich.<anchor n="151"
                        xml:id="d1578-f1"/> Fabela states, however, that he accepts the information
                    and will act upon it as in any case brought to attention by private parties.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1578-f1" n="151" xml:id="d1578-f1-content">
                <p>See, under Protection of Spanish subjects, Mr. Simpich’s No. 289 of Feb. 19; Mr.
                    Carothers’s Apr. 9, 7 p.m.; Apr. 11, 7 p.m.: Apr. 12, and Apr. 14; under
                    Protection of British subjects, Mr. Simpich’s Feb. 26, Feb. 28, and Mar. 11.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
